SECTION = r"""\section{The GameBoard: the way the algebra is computed with}\label{sec:gameboard}

The GameBoard is the way the algebra is computed with, not the object: a system of information transfer with costs, read in two ways, the detector's click a measurement and the host's view a diagnostic. This section states the law as one map with its postulates, the state it acts on under the record kinds of Sections~\ref{sec:algebra} and~\ref{sec:massive}, the six operations as the engine runs them, the read-out, the code and the ledger; every sentence is the algebra document's \cite[chapters 2, 3 and 8]{algebra}. The law as the engine ran it before 2026-09-23, the rows that hop whole with their wheel, their rungs and their components, is its record \cite{records}.

\subsection{The law and its implementation}\label{sec:law}

\paragraph{The one map.} The law is the map of Eq.~\eqref{eq:map} applied at every Node at every interval, per component $s$ of the state vector, each with its declared rate $r$ and wall $d$: the component is translated by its rate, counted in walls, capped at $a = 1$ where a cap is declared and uncapped elsewhere (the whole part $\lfloor |s|/d \rfloor$ with the sign), and reduced by the walls it holds; every wall counted is an event, and nothing else happens. One declared variant of the count, the centred step, takes the nearest whole number the accumulator holds, $(|s| + \lfloor d/2 \rfloor)$ divided by $d$ with the sign; it is named where a rule uses it. Where the rate is a constant of the world (the linear block) every component has the closed form $s(t) = \lfloor s_0 + rt \rfloor$, $r$ the rate as a fraction of the wall, so a record's state at any interval is a formula of its birth and its age; where the rate is a function of what arrives (the feedback block: the push, the drive, the coupling of the two kinds) the map is iterated and its continuum limit is the differential equation $d\mathbf s/dt = \mathbf r(\mathbf s)$. The read-out is one comparison, the click \cite[chapter 2]{algebra}.

\paragraph{Rules, parameters, initial conditions.} The law is stated as rules, apart from the parameters and the initial conditions a world supplies. The rules: (P1) every quantity of the state is a bounded integer and every operation integer arithmetic, no real number, root or floating point at run time (the boundedness a property of the declared worlds over their declared ticks, guarded by the run-time amplitude bound: the light pair puts the pace at the six-neighbour rule's causal limit, $c^2 = 1/3$, so on a full three-dimensional board the two modes $\mathbf k = 0$, a uniform level, and $(\pi, \pi, \pi)$, the checkerboard, are marginal, double roots, growing at most linearly if inserted, and no GO world inserts either, and what a sharp edge excites of them on a full board the run-time bound watches; on a chain or a layer the band edge lies inside the band); (P2) space is a cubic array of Nodes, each joined to six neighbours by Links through directional Ports, a Node's complete local information its NodeState, time a sequence of intervals; (P3) the rates and walls of the map are made of the six operations of Section~\ref{sec:intro} and nothing else; (P4) a rule reads its own record and the six neighbours; nothing is kept at a Node beyond the events there, no register or draw, and the remainder $r$ of Eq.~\eqref{eq:massive} is a component of the record's own state (the pair travels with the record \cite[8.8]{algebra}), not a register at the Node; (P5) no row or body crosses more than one Link per interval; (P6) a record is read out once, by one comparison, at the click, the one step that deletes, and the click of a pair is one gather of one record from both settings, the law's one non-local operation. Beside P6, once: the pair is one record with two arms (Definition~\ref{def:click}, the record $\psi = (00) + (11)$ of rank $2$, each arm carrying the weights, nothing of one arm written on the other); the completion is one gather at the completion interval, no interval crosses between the arms and no arm's history is altered; the counts' no-signalling follows from the table's symmetry (Theorem~\ref{th:marginals}); the completion is an operation of the law that relaxes P4 at that one step only, said so and not hidden. The parameters (P7, P8): the circle $\Nphi$ and its tables at $1/256$, the pair $[\mathrm{num}, \mathrm{den}]$ of each record kind with its pitch, light the value $[1, 1]$ (Eq.~\eqref{eq:massive}), the rung $W$ of each detector, the cells of each block with its lowered pair, the take of each absorbing object, and the roundings declared at load; the initial conditions: the box and its boundaries, the blocks with their momenta, the lamps and the detectors of the world file, and the seed, the bound mode's integer profile over the whole board, the engine reading integers \cite[8.7]{algebra}. The law of this paper is the runtime at the commit Appendix~\ref{app:reproduction} names. The rules chosen among few (P9) are assumptions, not derivations, each named where it enters and each marked in the algebra document as carried, proved or computed and not proved: the rule with the pair per kind, carried from the design, its band and its two paces proved; the click's definition at the rung, carried on the author's word; the one formula of a block's motion, carried from the continuum, its two limits proved; the stress of light at a block's outer Ports as the wave's momentum flux, the design's declaration; and the bijection of the interval, the design's proof carried (Section~\ref{sec:massive}). One axiom of the apparatus (P10): the click stores one pointer per set, the least-rank member of the family Theorem~\ref{th:gleason} forces, which is Born's form with the fundamental harmonic; which harmonic is a relabelling of the declared rate, and the harmonic constants are not derived. One assumption of the frame (P11): the GameBoard, Inside, is read only through its emitters and detectors, Outside; every result Outside is a click, a number of the board's state is never a reading, and every comparison with experiment is a comparison of clicks with readings; a measurement is itself an event of the board, an emitter putting a record on it and a detector ending the record at the click, the one step that deletes Inside and the one row that Outside gains. Nothing outside this list is assumed.

\paragraph{The state.} The GameBoard is a box of Nodes in $\Z^3$, each joined to six neighbours by Links through six Ports, an axis periodic or open; time is the interval $t \in \Z$; the state at an interval is a vector $\mathbf s$ of bounded integers on a product of circles and lines. A Node's complete local information is its NodeState: per record kind present, the record's row, its two levels and its remainder $(a_{\mathrm{now}}, a_{\mathrm{before}}, r)$ of Eq.~\eqref{eq:massive}; at a block's cell, the block's lowered pair, its pointer in the units of the conserved form and its count; nothing else, no register, no draw, no field beyond the records there; beside the click's gather the model declares two other non-local objects, a body's cells acting as one (the foreign object's extent, an input of kind 3, a detector of itself across its own cells) and the record's own ledger (its pointer per cell, its $u$, its norm), the record's state travelling with it and not a Node's, so that a Node holds nothing but the rows present at it and the locality claim stops at the Inside's verbs \cite[2.11, 8.1, 8.6]{algebra}. A block carries its cells, its momentum $\mathbf p$ in $\Z^3$ and its step's accumulator per axis with its remainder (Section~\ref{sec:massive}). This paper states one law, the record kind; the rows that hop are its record. The rows that hop, a tuple (Node, direction, age, phase, emitter, content, record, label, amount, multiplicity) moving one Link per interval on a digital line, are the engine as built before 2026-09-23, kept as their record \cite[2.11]{algebra}: Definition~\ref{def:row} and the theorems stated on them (Theorems~\ref{th:isometry}, \ref{th:bijection}, \ref{th:gleason}, \ref{th:marginals} and~\ref{th:bell}) stand as proved, on the objects they name.

\paragraph{The six operations as the engine runs them.} One interval applies, in order, (T) on every accumulator; (D), whose whole part is the event; (B) at the push and at the click; (G) and (E) where records are summed at one Node and where they end; and (P) at a collision \cite[2.11]{algebra}. In symbols, one line each \cite[2.1 to 2.6]{algebra}: (T) $x \mapsto x + r$ on $\Z^k$ or on the torus, every count of the law, the translation group of the torus this verb on Nodes; (B) a moment sum over the neighbourhood's records, $\mathbf u^{\mathsf T}\mathbf C\mathbf v$ with $\mathbf C$ declared, the push's rate bilinear in the state, the click's weight $\mathbf f^{\mathsf T}\mathbf G\mathbf f$ with $\mathbf G = \mathbf E^{\mathsf T}\mathbf E$ this form on the record's element, nothing squared as a step of its own; (G) the merge $f \mapsto f + g$ in $\Z[\Z_{\Nphi}]$ with the cancel $[p + \Nphi/2] = -[p]$, the quotient by $x^{\Nphi/2} + 1$, which for $\Nphi$ a power of two is the ring of cyclotomic integers $\Z[\zeta_{\Nphi}]$, a free $\Z$-module of rank $\Nphi/2$, two arms' elements multiplying by the ring's convolution; (P) a permutation of directions, labels or Nodes, never of contents (a gate, a tie); (E) the exact evaluation $\mathrm{ev} : \Z[\Z_{\Nphi}] \to \Z[\zeta_{\Nphi}]$, a surjective ring homomorphism whose kernel is the ideal of the cancel, so that $\Z[\Z_{\Nphi}]/\ker \mathrm{ev} = \Z[\zeta_{\Nphi}]$ exactly, and beside it the built evaluation, the tables at the scale $256$, a $\Z$-linear map into $\Z^2$ that is not a ring homomorphism, its kernel larger than the cancel's (at $\Nphi = 64$, $\mathbf E(e_1)^2 = (64400, 12750)$ against $256\,\mathbf E(e_2) = (64256, 12800)$, COMPUTATION), the exact line the algebra's and the rounding the engine's declared constant; (D) the signed truncating division with the remainder kept in $(-d, d)$, the code's wording in force, the Euclidean division on every non-negative accumulator, and the comparison as part of the verb, a division whose quotient is $0$ or $1$ and whose remainder is not read. What is not one of the six: a root of the state at run time, the seventh verb, not admitted, which Lorentz's gamma on a body's own counter would need (Section~\ref{sec:click}); a rounded constant multiplying a record in flight is a declared rounding at load, not a verb; no float, no true division, no draw \cite[2.7]{algebra}.

\paragraph{The three tests, rule by rule.} A rule enters the law only if it is generic (one primitive with declared integers, no family name or kind, the engine branching on no name), vector (one of the six verbs on the state vector, its rate at most bilinear in the state, no root, no float, no rounding at run time beyond the ones declared at load) and local (its own record and the six neighbouring Nodes, fixed work and storage for a fixed $K$, nothing kept at a Node); generic means commuting with the $48$ \cite[2.8]{algebra}. Each rule of Section~\ref{sec:massive} passes the three and carries its mark \cite[8.10]{algebra}: the rule with the pair on the six reads, (B), (T) and (D), the band and the two paces proved, the range-one bound computed and not proved; the conserved form, a bilinear form of the two levels, proved on every board with the remainders' identity; the well of the pair on declared cells, the threshold and the tail computed and not proved, the norm bound proved for the declared pairs whose band lies strictly inside the stability limit ($[800, 809]$ bounded); under $[1, 1]$ the $k = 0$ and $(\pi, \pi, \pi)$ modes are marginal and grow linearly, neither inserted by a declared world, P1's boundedness per declared world; the motion, the one formula carried, its two limits proved; the coupling, (B) linear in the other kind's two columns and one (D) per row, the Euler--Lagrange scheme and the invariant $J$ with its remainder identity proved, the index and the pump computed and not proved; the click across the block's cells at $W$, (E), the bilinear form and (D)'s comparison, the definition carried; the take, a declaration, no identity; the seed, the standing start proved; the direction of time, (D) with the ceiling, the bijection carried and its inverse exact; the block's momentum, step and push, the cadence and the bound proved as identities of the accumulator, the stress carried as the design's declaration; the force between two blocks through light, the closed form carried, on the GameBoard computed and not proved.

\paragraph{The read-out.} The click is the evaluation (E) of a body's own record on its cells at the declared rung $W$: light arriving at the block's cells drives the block's record through the coupling, the block's pointer accumulates its own record's motion across all its cells in the units of the conserved form, and the click is the comparison $W \times (\text{the pointer}) \ge (\text{the record's norm})$, integers both, in the block's own clock (its own record's cycles across its cells, not a count of clicks); the click line carries the block's own count and the light record's birth stamp. Light clicks only at a detector set, a declared set of Nodes with its rung $W$; at a massive body's cells light does not click but drives the body's record through the coupling, and the body's own click reads that; a free Node has no rung, no count and no reading; the verbs are lossless, light passes on, and the click needs no sink; where a world must absorb it declares a take, a damping pair on light's row at the cells of an object declared absorbing, a declaration of the world and not the law's \cite[8.6]{algebra}. A click is an action, not a passive read: the record ends at the detector, its content enters the detector's own record, and the detector's count advances, the click stamped with that count \cite[3.1]{algebra}. Between a birth and a click the interval is a bijection, its inverse exact (Section~\ref{sec:massive}, the direction of time; for the rows that hop, Theorem~\ref{th:bijection}); the click is the one deletion, and the pair's gather the one non-local step (P6).

\paragraph{The code as the law's runtime.} Every registered world is run from its world file with its pin written before the run and its source fingerprint (Appendix~\ref{app:reproduction}); the books balance at every interval in every run. The design's scripts, each printing its record beside the design and none an engine run, compute the band and the corner, the conserved forms $I$ and $J$ with their remainders' terms, the block's threshold, the board's margin, the index, the self-trapping of light, the block's clock in motion, the layer and the moving pins, the light clock's relay, the moving index, the well's spectrum and the time reversal \cite[8.10]{algebra}; what they compute and do not prove is marked so above. These are gates on the code, not measurements; the replications and the hand-worked update of the engine before 2026-09-23 are its record \cite{records}.

"""
